(Section 4.2: Kinetic Energy and Work-Energy Theorem) Tj
T* (Kinetic energy is the energy an object possesses due to its motion.) Tj
T* (The formula for translational kinetic energy is KE = 0.5 * m * v^2, where m is mass in kilograms \(kg\) and v is velocity in meters per second \(m/s\).) Tj
T* (Kinetic energy is measured in Joules \(J\). Doubling the velocity of a moving object quadruples its kinetic energy.) Tj
ET
endstream
